<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muradid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1613–1702</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muradid dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> as hereditary beys under Ottoman suzerainty from 1613 to 1702. Founded by Murad Bey, a Corsican-born mamluk, it grew stronger under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammuda-pasha-bey">Hammuda Pasha Bey</a> and eclipsed the deys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>. Succession wars within the family from 1675 and invasions from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> weakened it; the last Muradid bey was killed in 1702, and in 1705 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husainid-dynasty">Husainid dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muradid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Muradid dynasty" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rayan54 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Tunisia_(1620).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
